{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible-light-mediated Minisci C-H alkylation of N-heteroarenes using unactivated primary, secondary, and tertiary alkyl halides. The method utilizes an iridium photoredox catalyst, tris(trimethylsilyl)silane (TTMS) as a halogen-abstraction agent, and molecular oxygen as the terminal oxidant under mild conditions. This protocol enables the late-stage functionalization of complex natural products and drugs.",
